WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.957 --> 00:00:15.589
The next morning everyone was awake early.

2
00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:20.999
The children sprang about the tree house like monkeys while I sat beneath the great tree.

3
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.951
"What should we do next, Father?" Franz called down to me.

4
00:00:24.952 --> 00:00:27.643
"What do you want us to do today?"

5
00:00:27.644 --> 00:00:31.818
"Rest, my boys," I replied. "Rest."

6
00:00:31.819 --> 00:00:36.072
"Rest?" Franz repeated. "Why should we rest?"

7
00:00:36.073 --> 00:00:40.390
"It's Sunday. Come down here, please."

8
00:00:40.396 --> 00:00:44.872
"Is it really Sunday?" asked Jack when he'd climbed down the ladder.

9
00:00:44.873 --> 00:00:47.882
"How jolly! I won't do any work.

10
00:00:47.883 --> 00:00:51.287
I'll take a bow and arrow and prowl through the woods.

11
00:00:51.288 --> 00:00:54.756
And we'll climb about the tree and have fun all day."

12
00:00:54.757 --> 00:00:57.563
"That's not resting, Jack," I pointed out.

13
00:00:57.564 --> 00:01:00.976
"That's not the way you usually spend Sundays."

14
00:01:00.977 --> 00:01:04.577
"I usually go to church, but we don't have a church here."

15
00:01:04.578 --> 00:01:09.358
"And we don't have a clergyman or an organ," added little Franz.

16
00:01:09.359 --> 00:01:12.757
"We can still offer thanks for our new home," I said.

17
00:01:12.758 --> 00:01:15.577
"Come, everyone, gather around me."

18
00:01:15.578 --> 00:01:20.800
After I led my family in some prayers and hymns, the boys were free to do as they liked.

19
00:01:20.801 --> 00:01:23.467
I continued to sit under our tree.

20
00:01:23.468 --> 00:01:28.061
A few birds came to feed on the figs, which were just beginning to ripen.

21
00:01:28.062 --> 00:01:32.874
I realized that as more figs ripened, more birds would come.

22
00:01:32.875 --> 00:01:39.007
If we could preserve some birds, we could eat them during the rainy season when food might be scarce.

23
00:01:39.008 --> 00:01:44.885
Relieved that I'd thought of a way to provide food for my family, I enjoyed my morning in the shade.

24
00:01:44.886 --> 00:01:49.697
During lunch I proposed that we name all the places we'd visited since we arrived.

25
00:01:49.698 --> 00:01:53.993
"We'll feel more at home if these places have names," I said.

26
00:01:53.994 --> 00:01:57.310
"Let's start by naming the bay where we landed."

27
00:01:57.311 --> 00:01:59.663
"Oyster Bay," said Fritz.

28
00:01:59.664 --> 00:02:02.282
"No, no," protested Jack.

29
00:02:02.283 --> 00:02:06.365
"Lobster Bay, in memory of the fellow who grabbed my leg."

30
00:02:06.366 --> 00:02:10.044
"I think we should call it Safety Bay," said my wife.

31
00:02:10.045 --> 00:02:14.612
"It will be a token of our gratitude for a safe escape from the ship."

32
00:02:14.613 --> 00:02:16.856
"I like it!" said Ernest.

33
00:02:16.857 --> 00:02:21.666
The others agreed, and so the bay was known as Safety Bay from that moment on.

34
00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:25.842
We easily decided on Tentholm for the place where we first lived.

35
00:02:25.843 --> 00:02:31.860
Many names were proposed for our tree house, but we finally decided on Falconhurst.

36
00:02:31.861 --> 00:02:37.349
We spent the rest of the day quietly.

37
00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:42.044
The following morning I proposed an expedition to Tentholm.

38
00:02:42.045 --> 00:02:44.031
We went by a different route.

39
00:02:44.032 --> 00:02:46.639
The boys roamed ahead of my wife and me.

40
00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:50.049
Knips the monkey rode along on Juno the dog.

41
00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:57.565
Soon I heard a joyful shout, and Ernest came running toward me at full speed, followed by his brothers.

42
00:02:57.566 --> 00:03:00.063
He held out a plant for me to see.

43
00:03:00.064 --> 00:03:04.541
"Potatoes! Potatoes, Father!" Ernest was gasping for breath.

44
00:03:04.542 --> 00:03:10.386
"Yes," said Jack. "Acres and acres of potatoes. Come look at them."

45
00:03:10.387 --> 00:03:12.695
My wife and I hurried to the spot.

46
00:03:12.696 --> 00:03:17.966
There indeed was a great area of land covered with potato plants.

47
00:03:17.967 --> 00:03:21.341
"Ernest, you've made a great discovery," I said.

48
00:03:21.342 --> 00:03:24.992
"With all these potatoes, we'll always have something to eat."

49
00:03:24.993 --> 00:03:29.172
"Ernest may have the honor of discovering the potatoes," said Jack.

50
00:03:29.173 --> 00:03:32.942
"But I'll have the honor of being the first to harvest them."

51
00:03:32.943 --> 00:03:36.093
So he set to work digging potatoes with his hands.

52
00:03:36.094 --> 00:03:40.798
Knips followed his example and soon had a pile of potatoes beside him.

53
00:03:40.799 --> 00:03:47.014
Everyone began digging, and we didn't stop until we'd filled every bag, pouch, and pocket.

54
00:03:47.015 --> 00:03:52.100
We pushed on to Tentholm, loaded down with potatoes but happy with our find.

55
00:03:52.101 --> 00:03:58.730
Along the way the boys pestered me for the names and uses of the many strange plants and trees we passed.

56
00:03:58.731 --> 00:04:03.365
I recognized some of them, but there were many others that I couldn't identify.

57
00:04:03.366 --> 00:04:08.643
Everything was safe at Tentholm, and we began gathering what we wanted to take back.

58
00:04:08.644 --> 00:04:13.337
I collected a fresh supply of salt, and my wife wanted to make butter.

59
00:04:13.338 --> 00:04:18.675
Jack and Ernest ran down to the beach to capture the geese and ducks that we'd left behind.

60
00:04:18.676 --> 00:04:23.368
The birds were out on the water, and nothing could persuade them to come ashore.

61
00:04:23.369 --> 00:04:28.595
"I know!" said Ernest. "Let's ask Mother for some cheese and string."

62
00:04:28.596 --> 00:04:32.856
"Cheese and string?" said Jack. "Who will eat that?"

63
00:04:32.857 --> 00:04:37.763
"Just watch," said Ernest as he led Jack to the tent for supplies.

64
00:04:37.764 --> 00:04:43.820
Back at the beach, the boys broke off pieces of cheese and tied a long string around each one.

65
00:04:43.821 --> 00:04:48.621
Ernest threw the bait into the water, and the hungry birds instantly went after it.

66
00:04:48.622 --> 00:04:55.404
With a little maneuvering, he got the birds onshore, where Jack caught them and tied their feet together.

67
00:04:55.405 --> 00:04:59.283
We soon set off for Falconhurst.

68
00:04:59.284 --> 00:05:03.119
After a pleasant walk, we were back at our tree house.

69
00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:05.609
I released the birds into our stream.

70
00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:14.259
After a delicious supper of potatoes, milk, and butter, we went to bed.
